id: pm-9djr6d
title: Edit linked-test metadata in place with preserved provenance and atomic history
description: "Implement the complete GH1419 linked-test editor under the existing universal metadata reference lineage. Patch only explicit supported metadata fields; retain list position, immutable creation provenance and unchanged fields; stamp editor identity and time; reject empty or ambiguous selectors atomically; expose the same SDK operation through CLI and MCP."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T15:39:56.760Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T19:50:56.291Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T19:31:12.268Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T19:31:12.268Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: CLI and SDK edit one linked test by exact selector or one-based index; unchanged fields and original provenance survive; changed edit writes one field-level history event and editor metadata; equal retry preserves authoritative bytes; absent or ambiguous selectors refuse without mutation; invalid context patches are refused before persistence; command changes require fresh provenance/trust rather than preserving authorization; packed Node and Bun transports agree.
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-gh1381
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Shared SDK metadata patches preserve ordering, command and creation provenance, use granular locked history and byte-stable no-op retries. CLI and MCP expose the same selectors. New serialized edit inputs obey shared telemetry redaction; correlation digests remain intact."
expected_result: "Correct one linked test without reconstructing it, preserve trust and provenance rules, and retain useful telemetry without arbitrary metadata payloads."
actual_result: "All three linked commands pass. Canonical sandboxed coverage passes 10,166 tests in 798 files with 68097/68097 statements, 52238/52238 branches, 14040/14040 functions and 64757/64757 lines. Typecheck, ESLint and docstring gate pass. The isolated pre-fix control fails at redacted and max capture, and the same regression plus all 48 telemetry runtime cases pass after the guard. Base archive remains below its unchanged ceiling; final static and regenerated-changelog consumers are verified before push."
